# Rust build artifacts. The leading slash restricts this to the target
# directory at the workspace root (so crates/*/target is not ignored by mistake).
/target

# Built wasm. `scripts/size.sh` writes under target/, so nothing normally lands
# here, but adding a 250 KB binary by accident is easy enough to be worth a net.
# If you ever want to commit a distributable, either `git add -f` that single
# file or add a `!path/to/file.wasm` line here.
*.wasm

# Where CI `tee`s the output of scripts/size.sh.
size-report.txt

# JS host layer. There are no npm dependencies or bundles today; this is for when there are.
node_modules
dist

# Scratch git worktrees created by Claude Code. They hold checkouts of this same
# repository, so committing them would nest a working tree inside the history.
.claude/worktrees/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Cargo.lock **is tracked**.
# Besides this being a workspace containing a binary (the ahiru CLI), wasm size
# is a hard constraint here, and without a reproducible dependency graph there
# is no way to track down the cause of a size regression.
#
# The generated files under tests/data/ **are tracked** too.
# ahiru-core's unit tests read them directly, so ignoring them would make
# `cargo test` fail on a clean clone. Keeping the tests independent of external
# tools (duckdb) won out. Use scripts/gen-testdata.sh to regenerate them.
